# Bug #163 Phase 2: round-trip test for the os9-link post-link emitter.
#
# Asserts that:
#   1. os9-link wraps a hand-crafted flat binary into a valid OS-9 module.
#   2. os9-module-check (the Phase 1 validator) accepts that module.
#   3. Specific bytes of the produced module are correct — guards against
#      any silent algorithm drift (header parity, CRC trailer, fcs name
#      encoding).
#
# The pair os9-link + os9-module-check is meant to round-trip: a change
# that breaks os9-link's header layout, parity, or CRC will fail at the
# validator step, and a change that loosens os9-module-check's checks
# will fail at the byte-level FileCheck stage below.

# Hand-craft a minimal program-module body that just exits:
#   ldb #0    ; $C6 $00
#   swi2      ; $10 $3F
#   fcb $06   ; F$Exit
# (`printf '\xNN'` is non-portable across lit's shell, so use python3.)
RUN: python3 -c "import sys; sys.stdout.buffer.write(bytes([0xc6,0x00,0x10,0x3f,0x06]))" > %t.bin

# Wrap as an OS-9 program module.  Name "hello", exec at +13 (the first
# body byte), 256-byte M$Mem allocation.
RUN: %S/../../../../tools/os9-link %t.bin --name hello --exec 13 --mem 256 -o %t.os9

# The Phase 1 validator must accept the result.
RUN: %S/../../../../tools/os9-module-check %t.os9 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=VALIDATOR

# Byte-exact assertion on the produced module.  Layout (26 bytes total):
#   00..0C  13-byte header: 87 cd 00 1a 00 12 11 a0 0c 00 0d 01 00
#                           |sync|size|name_off|type|attr|par|exec|mem|
#   0D..11   5-byte body: c6 00 10 3f 06
#   12..16   5-byte fcs name "hell" + 'o' with bit-7 set (ef = 6f|80)
#   17..19   3-byte CRC: 42 e4 a1  (~body_CRC; full module CRC = $800FE3)
RUN: od -A n -t x1 %t.os9 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=BYTES

VALIDATOR: OK ({{[0-9]+}} bytes)
VALIDATOR: type/lang: $11 (Prgrm|Objct)
VALIDATOR: attr/rev:  $A0 (ReEnt|ModNat, rev=0)
VALIDATOR: exec offset: $000D (13)
VALIDATOR: mem size:    $0100 (256)
VALIDATOR: name: "hello"
VALIDATOR: CRC: valid (full CRC = $800FE3)

BYTES: 87 cd 00 1a 00 12 11 a0 0c 00 0d 01 00 c6 00 10
BYTES: 3f 06 68 65 6c 6c ef 42 e4 a1
